<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Overrides, for a brand whose manifest says features.esim is false.

     These four strings are the ONLY ones in main/res that name the eSIM
     store's domain. A brand that sells no eSIM shipped all four, in every
     language, so the sister domain was readable in its resources.arsc long
     after it was gone from the dex. A runtime flag does not remove a string
     from a binary.

     WHY AN OVERRIDE AND NOT A MOVE. All four are referenced from
     src/main/java (ShopScreens.kt:621, ShopCheckout.kt:276 and :466,
     ShopApi.kt:83,90, AccountTab.kt:330), which every brand compiles.
     Removing them from main is an Unresolved reference on every brand. The
     resource merge lets the flavour value win instead, so main is untouched,
     Kotlin is untouched and the R class is stable. src/probe/res is wired the
     same way (build.gradle.kts).

     WHY ALL 39 QUALIFIERS. A locale qualifier beats a source-set override. A
     copy in values/ alone still loses to main/res/values-fa/, and the domain
     would ship in Persian anyway. This is the rule that once showed
     "RostamVPN" to every Persian device on RedVPN.

     WHY NO TRANSLATION. Every one of these is unreachable when the flag is
     false: AccountTab.kt:330 sits inside a dialog behind the FEATURE_ESIM
     gate at :132, and the shop screens are only reachable through openEsim(),
     which VpnViewModel.kt:2374 refuses. Identical neutral English in all 39
     is adequate, and inventing 38 translations of dead copy is not.

     shop_payment_safe MUST keep exactly one %1$s. A second specifier is an
     IllegalFormatException in that language only. -->
<resources>
    <string name="tabs_esim_code_body">Enter this code on another phone to see your eSIMs there. Keep it private: it opens your eSIMs\' install codes.</string>
    <string name="shop_delivered">Plans are delivered by our eSIM partner.</string>
    <string name="shop_unexpected">We got an unexpected answer from the store. Update the app or try again.</string>
    <string name="shop_payment_safe">Your payment is safe. Contact support with order %1$s and we\'ll fix it or refund you.</string>
</resources>
